# F2 (W4-WIN-FINAL): the CPU window settles a change as Visible only after the frame that holds it was
# delivered through SDL_UpdateTexture, SDL_RenderTexture and SDL_RenderPresent. Each stage is made to report
# failure in turn (the real call is made, its result overridden: `fail STAGE`); with fresh chunks the applied
# command must stay pending (NotPresented), the window keeps drawing and handling input, and releasing the
# failure lets the SAME command become Visible after a delivered frame. Run by tools/test/viewer_wiring.py
# (CPU renderer, SDL dummy driver) with --expect-stderr for the diagnostic of each stage.
look 1140 516
key b
select 1307
rotate 0
wait frames 60

# ---- baseline: normal delivery settles the change -----------------------------------------------
click 1140 516
wait outcome
wait drawn
expect visibility Visible
checkpoint baseline_visible

# ---- SDL_UpdateTexture fails --------------------------------------------------------------------
fail update
click 1156 516
wait outcome
expect outcome Applied
wait visibility NotPresented
wait frames 20
expect failing update
expect visibility NotPresented
# Input and the sim go on meanwhile: a second edit is applied, and it is pending too.
click 1164 516
wait outcome
expect outcome Applied
wait frames 20
expect visibility NotPresented
checkpoint update_failing
pass update
wait drawn
expect visibility Visible
checkpoint update_released

# ---- SDL_RenderTexture fails --------------------------------------------------------------------
fail submit
click 1172 516
wait outcome
wait visibility NotPresented
wait frames 20
expect failing submit
expect visibility NotPresented
checkpoint submit_failing
pass submit
wait drawn
expect visibility Visible
checkpoint submit_released

# ---- SDL_RenderPresent fails --------------------------------------------------------------------
fail present
click 1180 516
wait outcome
wait visibility NotPresented
wait frames 20
expect failing present
expect visibility NotPresented
# A failing delivery retries at the 100 ms back-off, not at the loop's rate: about ten frames a second.
note frames
wait ms 1000
expect frames at-most 30
checkpoint present_failing
pass present
wait drawn
expect visibility Visible
checkpoint present_released
quit
